.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt URTSX 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm urtsx
.Nd Realtek USB SD card host controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "urtsx* at uhub?"
.Cd "sdmmc* at urtsx?"
.Cd "ld* at sdmmc?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports the Realtek RTS5129 USB card reader with vendor ID 0x0bda
and product ID 0x0129.
It connects the controller to the
.Xr sdmmc 4
subsystem, which discovers the card and provides block devices through
.Xr ld 4 .
.Pp
The initial implementation supports SD memory cards at 3.3 volts,
with one data line and a maximum clock of 25 MHz.
It reads and writes one block at a time through the controller's 512-byte buffer.
The SD/MMC bus splits larger requests into single blocks.
Card detection uses a cached status value.
USB requests run in process context.
.Pp
Suspend stops card polling and powers off the slot after child devices drain I/O.
Resume restores the controller and reidentifies the card through the SD/MMC bus.
The bus checks the card identifier and geometry before it resumes the existing block device.
If the card is missing, changed or unavailable, the block device remains suspended.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
Write transfers wait for the card's physical busy signal to clear.
An uncertain write failure reaches the caller without an automatic block retry.
.Pp
The driver rejects erase commands, lock commands and persistent switches.
The reported write-protect switch state remains the physical card state.
.Pp
SDIO, MMC, UHS, 1.8-volt signalling and multiblock transfers are not supported.
Memory Stick and xD media are not supported.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ld 4 ,
.Xr rtsx 4 ,
.Xr sdmmc 4 ,
.Xr usb 4
